# Code Hygiene Standards

## 1. Code Style
- Laravel Pint (default preset). `vendor/bin/pint --test` must pass before a PR.

## 2. Punctuation & Character Policy
- Use plain ASCII characters in new code, comments, Blade views, and translation files.
- Prohibited: smart curly quotes (`“`, `”`, `‘`, `’`), em-dash (`—`), en-dash (`–`), and Unicode ellipsis (`…`).
- Permitted: plain straight quotes (`"` and `'`), ASCII hyphens (`-`), and ASCII dots (`...`).

## 3. Timezone & DateTime Safety
- Store timestamps in UTC (`config/app.php` timezone is `UTC`).
- Convert to the user's `users.timezone` only when displaying.
- For calendar dates without time components (birth date, availability dates), use `Y-m-d` strings or `date` casts to avoid off-by-one errors.

## 4. Error Handling & Security
- Validate input with Form Requests or `$request->validate()`.
- Protect routes with the right role middleware (Spatie) and check record ownership.
- Do not expose raw database errors or stack traces to end users.
